  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "Even after the named affine-family and Lucas/Kummer prerequisites, the proof must construct a divided iterated directional-difference constraint, bound its support, and prove its simultaneous acceptance and rejection behavior by finite-field power sums and carry-free coefficients. The complete authored product/union constructions at1174–1392 then preserve the explicit locality bound, while the new affine monomial-transfer proof at1398–1479 makes the entire orbit reject every border monomial. These coupled sparse-constraint and orbit-characterization obligations form one H2 task above routine finite-field interpolation or direct application of a testing theorem.",
  "source_scope_note": "Exact original Main Theorem1.1 only, for every finite field q=p^s, degree d and number of variables n, with original c_q<=3q^4, query bound and epsilon=min{1/2,1/((2k+1)(k-1))}. Original Reed-Muller model and soundness convention, all constraint/single-orbit/degree/shadow/border definitions, full border reduction, divided-directional-difference sparse constraint and every support/acceptance/rejection proof, product and union extensions with exact locality estimate, complete affine monomial-transfer argument and primary closing are retained. Named Kaufman-Sudan single-orbit testability and monomial extraction/spread, Lucas/Kummer and finite-field power sums are stated prerequisites; all new source-local construction is supplied. The tiny sparsity-tightness addendum remains uncounted author context. Spanning-weight and parameter specializations are unselected and uncounted. All-page source/output QA completed and exact final actual logs checked. Source-material candidate only; no admission/remote-delivery credit.",
  "source_quirks_note": "The source directional-derivative definition and its iterated sum at913 retain the exact original (-1)^{|I|+1} formula. The subsection PDF-string alternative at875 retains p(p-q/p) while its visible mathematical title is p(q-q/p). Native1095 retains its displayed tilde-m exponents and native1084 retains q-1 in the product display; all adjoining original context and formulas are preserved without mathematical correction or refereeing.",
